CLASS:: MP1Decode
SUMMARY:: Synthesize editable fields or packed bytes
CATEGORIES:: UGens>MPEG Audio
RELATED:: Guides/MPEGAudio, Classes/MP1Encode, Classes/MPEGDecodeOutput

DESCRIPTION::
A field decoder can audition a target bitrate. A byte decoder follows the incoming stream. Both inputs support holds.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: ar
Synthesize a field stream. Bitrate 0 reads the supplied fields directly.

ARGUMENT:: fields
An MPEGFrame for the same layer. Encoders, readers and the MPEGFrame constructors all supply this type.

ARGUMENT:: bitrate
Requested kb/s. A control or audio-rate signal can change it at a frame boundary. The object selects the nearest legal rate.

ARGUMENT:: freeze
A gate of 1 holds the last frame, including its level. Set to 0 to follow live data.

ARGUMENT:: holds
Per-band gates. A single value broadcasts, 32 values address a bank, and 64 values address left and right independently.

ARGUMENT:: holdMode
Use a symbol, code::\coeff:: or code::\level::, or a signal carrying 0 or 1. Level mode preserves the held band level.

ARGUMENT:: downsample
Native clock divisor from 1 to 6. A reader samples this at start. Connected field streams preserve the original codec clock.

ARGUMENT:: normalized
Set to 1 for bipolar words in the range −1 to 1. The default expects signed codec integers.

RETURNS:: Mono PCM or a stereo pair.

METHOD:: arInfo
Same arguments as ar. Also expose state, processed frame count and drops.

RETURNS:: An MPEGDecodeOutput.

METHOD:: bytes
Parse and play compressed audio frames at their header rate.

ARGUMENT:: bytes
An array of 1 to 64 byte signals, usually the eight lanes from a source’s code::bytes:: member. Each lane carries 0–255 or −1 for idle.

ARGUMENT:: channels
One or two output channels. Supply an integer when compiling the SynthDef.

ARGUMENT:: freeze
A gate of 1 holds the last frame, including its level. Set to 0 to follow live data.

ARGUMENT:: holds
Per-band gates. A single value broadcasts, 32 values address a bank, and 64 values address left and right independently.

ARGUMENT:: holdMode
Use a symbol, code::\coeff:: or code::\level::, or a signal carrying 0 or 1. Level mode preserves the held band level.

ARGUMENT:: downsample
Native clock divisor from 1 to 6. A reader samples this at start. Connected field streams preserve the original codec clock.

RETURNS:: Mono PCM or a stereo pair.

METHOD:: bytesInfo
Same arguments as bytes. Return PCM and status together.

RETURNS:: An MPEGDecodeOutput.

METHOD:: serial
Scan one Layer I word per host sample. See link::Classes/MP1Serial::.

EXAMPLES::
code::
{ var f = MPEGFrame.mp1(SinOsc.ar([2,3,5])*12); Limiter.ar(MP1Decode.ar(f),0.15) ! 2 }.play;
::
